morphtweaked.config.prop.childMorphs.comment=Can you acquire child mob morphs?\nDisabled by default due to improper morph transitions
morphtweaked.config.prop.playerMorphs.comment=Can you acquire player morphs?
morphtweaked.config.prop.bossMorphs.comment=Can you acquire boss morphs?This is disabled by default due to morphing issues with mobs like the EnderDragon, Twilight Forest's Hydra and Naga, etc.
morphtweaked.config.prop.blacklistedMobs.comment=Prevent players from acquiring these mobs as a morph.\nLeave blank to allow acquisition of all compatible mobs.\nFormatting is as follows: <class>, <class>, <class>\nExample: am2.entities.EntityBattleChicken, biomesoplenty.entities.EntityJungleSpider, thaumcraft.common.entities.monster.EntityWisp
morphtweaked.config.prop.listIsBlacklist.comment=Is the player list a blacklist or whitelist?\n0 = Blacklist - Listed players cannot use the Morph Skill\n1 = Whitelist - Listed players are the only ones who can use the Morph Skill
morphtweaked.config.prop.blackwhitelistedPlayers.comment=These players are on the list for Black/White listing for the Morph Skill.\nFormatting is as follows: <name>, <name>, <name>\nExample: Cojomax99, pahimar, ohaiiChun
morphtweaked.config.prop.loseMorphsOnDeath.comment=Will you lose your morphs on death?\n0 = No\n1 = Yes, all morphs\n2 = Yes, the morph you're currently using
morphtweaked.config.prop.instaMorph.comment=Will you insta-morph into a new morph acquired?
morphtweaked.config.prop.NBTStripper.comment=Enable mod mob NBT Stripping?\nThis support is mostly provided by the community and is not officially supported by the mod\nThe stripper was added to remove non-essential information from the Entity NBT to remove duplicate morphs.
morphtweaked.config.prop.useLocalResources.comment=Force the mod to use the local copy of resources in the config folder?\nThis is meant for debugging purposes and for modified local mod mob abilities mappings/NBT stripper.\nDo take note that mappings server and clientside are not synched so both ends will require the same mappings.
morphtweaked.config.prop.canSleepMorphed.comment=Can you sleep while morphed?
morphtweaked.config.prop.allowMorphSelection.comment=Requested by SoundLogic\nCan you open the morph GUI?
morphtweaked.config.prop.showPlayerLabel.comment=Show the player label of a morphed player?
morphtweaked.config.prop.abilities.comment=Enable abilities?
morphtweaked.config.prop.customPatchLink.comment=Redirect the mod to a different JSON patch location rather then the default patch hosted on GitHub.\nIf you would like to use the default, leave this blank.\nThis also affects NBTStripper.json.\nIf the link to your file is "https://raw.github.com/iChun/Morph/master/src/main/resources/assets/morph/mod/AbilitySupport.json", put "https://raw.github.com/iChun/Morph/master/src/main/resources/assets/morph/mod/", you cannot change the file name (eg: AbilitySupport.json) part of the link.
morphtweaked.config.prop.hostileAbilityMode.comment=Hostile Ability Modes\n0 = Off, hostile mobs attack you despite being morphed.\n1 = Hostile mobs do not attack you if you are a hostile mob.\n2 = Hostile mobs of different types do not attack you if you are a hostile mob but hostile mobs of the same kind do.\n3 = Hostile mobs of the same type do not attack you but hostile mobs of other types attack you.\n4 = Hostile mobs have a decreased detection range around you.\nIf you'd like to turn on Hostile Ability, I'd recommend Mode 2 (personal preference)
morphtweaked.config.prop.hostileAbilityDistanceCheck.comment=Hostile Ability Distance Check for Hostile Ability Mode 4\nYou have to be *this* close before hostile mobs know you are not one of them.\nDefault: 6
morphtweaked.config.prop.disableEarlyGameFlight.comment=Disable the flight ability until a player...\n0 = Enable early game flight\n1 = ...has reached the nether\n2 = ...has killed the Wither
morphtweaked.config.prop.disableEarlyGameFlightMode.comment=Disable Early Game Flight Mode\n0 = Serverwide toggle\n1 = Player specific toggle (Every player has to travel to the nether/kill a wither to get flight for themselves)
morphtweaked.config.prop.customMobToKillForFlight.comment=Change the requirement of killing a wither to a custom mob instead\nUse the full class name of the mob to make Morph bind to the killing of that mob type.(Eg: am2.entities.EntityBattleChicken)\nLeave blank to disable.\nNeeds Disable Early Game Flight set to killing the wither to work.
morphtweaked.config.prop.disabledAbilities.comment=What abilities to disable?\nYou need to use the Ability type (eg fly, witherResistance)\nSeparate each disabled ability with a comma\nEG: fly,swim,sink
morphtweaked.config.prop.keySelectorUp.comment=Key Code to go up on the selector\nDefault: 26 ([)
morphtweaked.config.prop.keySelectorDown.comment=Key Code to go down on the selector\nDefault: 27 (])
morphtweaked.config.prop.keySelectorLeft.comment=Key Code to go left on the selector\nDefault: 26 ([)
morphtweaked.config.prop.keySelectorRight.comment=Key Code to go right on the selector\nDefault: 27 (])
morphtweaked.config.prop.keySelectorSelect.comment=Key Code to select morph on the selector\nDefault: 28 (Enter/Return)
morphtweaked.config.prop.keySelectorCancel.comment=Key Code to close the selector\nDefault: 1 (Esc)
morphtweaked.config.prop.keySelectorRemoveMorph.comment=Key Code to remove morph on the selector.\nDelete also works by default\nDefault: 14 (Backspace)
morphtweaked.config.prop.keyFavourite.comment=Key Code to favourite/unfavourite morph on the selector and show the radial menu.\nDefault: 41 (` [also known as ~])
morphtweaked.config.prop.handRenderOverride.comment=Allow the mod to override player hand rendering?
morphtweaked.config.prop.showAbilitiesInGui.comment=Show the abilities the morph has in the GUI?
morphtweaked.config.prop.sortMorphs.comment=Sort the morphs in the GUI?\n0 = Order of acquisition (Server default)\n1 = Alphabetically (according to Operating System)\n2 = Alphabetically, and attempt to sort grouped morphs as well\n3 = Most recently used since connecting to the server
morphtweaked.config.prop.renderCrosshairInRadialMenu.comment=As per request, render the crosshair position when in the radial menu.

morphtweaked.command.demorph=/morph demorph [Spieler] [Erzwinge Zurückverwandlung sogar wenn offline (true/false)] - Verwandelt den Spieler zurück
morphtweaked.command.clear=/morph clear [Spieler] - Löscht alle möglichen Verwandlungen des Spielers
morphtweaked.command.morphtarget=/morph morphtarget [Spieler] - Versucht, den Spieler in das Lebewesen zu verwandeln, auf dass er gerade schaut
morphtweaked.command.addtolist=/morph whitelist <Spieler> - Fügt einen Spieler zu der Morph-Fähigkeits-Whitelist hinzu und aktiviert diese
morphtweaked.command.removefromlist=/morph unwhitelist <Spieler> - Entfernt einen Spieler von der Morph-Fähigkeits-Whitelist

